      ":question/problem": "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n(m+6)x+2=7\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $m?$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+6)x+2 & =7 \\\\ (m+6)x+2-2 & =7-2 \\\\ {{(m+6)}_{\u23df}}_{a}x & ={{5}_{\u23df}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nm+6=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m+6 & =0 \\\\ m & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
